  "analytic": [
    "Any R run is at most4 because four R restore the physical pose but make its read cell black. An interval beginning mid-run causes no exception: its remaining ordinary L edge was already present at the interval block entry.",
    "Ordinary R^r L blocks have r<=3, no w cycle birth, and bridge L deletion. The exact signed component inheritance applies independently of non-RRRR z-cycle births.",
    "Exceptional complete blocks are at most A + H + (beta+H), using GLOBAL w rank for nonbridge L deletions. A/H in a terminal unfinished run only make this upper bound weaker.",
    "Complete masses satisfy M_next<=3M+3 and M_j<=(m+2)3^j-2. Summing n_j<=M_j yields T<=4 sum n+5E+4<=2(m+2)(3^(E+1)-1)-3E-4<=6(m+2)3^E. All abandoned passive components remain charged to M.",
    "Each contained RRRR has a distinct fourth update creating a z unit cycle; each H is a cycle-birth update. Therefore A+2H<=3B, even if one update contributes to both. The logarithmic B bound is only for T>0; negative short-time lower bounds are harmless."
